  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0]) if h else 0\n\n    # Detect colors that form a complete row or complete column.\n    anchors = {}  # color -> (\"row\", r) or (\"col\", c)\n\n    for r in range(h):\n        color = grid[r][0]\n        if color != 0 and all(grid[r][c] == color for c in range(w)):\n            anchors[color] = (\"row\", r)\n\n    for c in range(w):\n        color = grid[0][c]\n        if color != 0 and all(grid[r][c] == color for r in range(h)):\n            anchors[color] = (\"col\", c)\n\n    # Start with an empty grid, then redraw only the anchored structures.\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n\n    # Draw the full anchor lines.\n    for color, (kind, idx) in anchors.items():\n        if kind == \"row\":\n            for c in range(w):\n                out[idx][c] = color\n        else:\n            for r in range(h):\n                out[r][idx] = color\n\n    # Project same-colored stray cells to the cell adjacent to the anchor line,\n    # on the same side they originally lie.\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            color = grid[r][c]\n            if color == 0 or color not in anchors:\n                continue\n\n            kind, idx = anchors[color]\n\n            # Skip cells that are already part of the full anchor line.\n            if kind == \"row\" and r == idx:\n                continue\n            if kind == \"col\" and c == idx:\n                continue\n\n            if kind == \"row\":\n                if r < idx and idx - 1 >= 0:\n                    out[idx - 1][c] = color\n                elif r > idx and idx + 1 < h:\n                    out[idx + 1][c] = color\n            else:  # kind == \"col\"\n                if c < idx and idx - 1 >= 0:\n                    out[r][idx - 1] = color\n                elif c > idx and idx + 1 < w:\n                    out[r][idx + 1] = color\n\n    return out",
